# R1113 (2026-10-23): agent scratch and stale code.
#
# `.aethercode/` holds probe scripts, maven logs and archived scratch from
# measurement rounds. It is not product and it grows without bound, so the whole
# directory is excluded rather than a growing list of patterns inside it.
.aethercode/

# These two preserve code that no longer compiles or no longer has an active
# gate. They are kept on disk deliberately (see plumb-dfa/pom.xml's surefire
# include list, which excludes ~120 legacy R-XXX files), but they are not part of
# the build and do not belong in history.
_backup_disabled_tests/
_backup_pre_existing_broken/

# Local distribution output from scripts/package-*.sh / dist-jlink-*.ps1
dist-jlink/
dist-test-package/

# R1113: IntelliJ project metadata. `*.iml`, `.idea/workspace.xml` and the other
# per-user files were already excluded above; these are the shared-looking ones
# (compiler.xml, encodings.xml, misc.xml) that would otherwise pin every contributor
# to one machine's JDK and encoding choices.
.idea/

# R1113: per-category raw scanner output. Regenerate with
#   python testcase/run_category.py testcase/<category> --per-file --keep-raw
testcase/**/_raw.ndjson
testcase/**/_raw.jsonl

# Python bytecode caches (scripts/gen_*.py are run in place).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The rule-doc generators write to docs/ now. This is the legacy output
# directory the generators used before they were repointed; it only appears
# if someone runs an older copy of the script.
doc/

# Classpath dumps written by `mvn dependency:build-classpath`. Maven resolves a
# relative -Dmdep.outputFile against the MODULE directory, so these land next to
# the module's pom.xml -- and they embed this machine's absolute repository
# paths, which are meaningless to anyone else.
**/main_cp.txt
**/cp.txt

# R1113: 746 MB of prior scan OUTPUT sitting under src/main/resources.
#
# plumb-dfa/src/main/resources/scripts holds the real corpus (614 .java fixtures).
# Alongside them are 22 .ndjson files that are captured *results* of earlier sweep
# runs -- r696_test_cwe89.ndjson alone is 98 MB, and r696_final_CWE319.ndjson,
# r696_scan/CWE319_*.ndjson, and the r697_{s01,s02,s03} copies across three output
# directories are byte-identical duplicates of one another.
#
# No source or test reads any of them (checked: zero references outside these files),
# they are not inputs to the build, and they are reproducible by re-running the scan.
# Committing them would put ~450 MB of duplicated binary-ish payload into permanent
# history, where it cannot be removed by a later .gitignore edit.
*.ndjson